      "designInstructions": "## Thumbfa.st — AI YouTube Thumbnail Generator\n\n### Brand Personality\nDark, focused, creator-centric. The app is a professional tool for YouTube creators who generate AI-powered thumbnails at speed. The UI disappears so thumbnails become the hero. Think DaVinci Resolve meets YouTube Studio — obsidian surfaces, crisp type, a red-orange accent that echoes YouTube's brand DNA. No gradients, no ornamentation. Craft is in the precision.\n\n### Color Palette\n- **Background** `(--background oklch(0.13 0 0))`: Near-pitch-black. Every page starts here.\n- **Surface** `(--surface oklch(0.18 0 0))`: Cards, panels, modals sit one level up.\n- **Surface-raised** `(--surface-raised oklch(0.22 0 0))`: Hover states, dropdowns, elevated panels.\n- **Border** `(--border oklch(0.28 0 0))`: Structural divisions. Always `1px`, never decorative.\n- **Primary** `(--primary oklch(0.628 0.258 29.23))`: The brand red-orange. CTAs, active badges, highlights. Never overused.\n- **Primary-muted** `(--primary-muted oklch(0.628 0.258 29.23 / 0.15))`: Tinted badge backgrounds, subtle accents.\n- **Text-primary** `(--text-primary oklch(0.95 0 0))`: Near-white. Titles, important labels.\n- **Text-secondary** `(--text-secondary oklch(0.65 0 0))`: Channel names, descriptions, meta.\n- **Text-muted** `(--text-muted oklch(0.45 0 0))`: Timestamps, counts, tertiary info.\n\n### Typography\nInter throughout. UI is information-dense, so sizing is restrained:\n- Card titles: `0.9375rem` (15px), `font-weight: 600`, tight `letter-spacing: -0.01em`, 2-line clamp.\n- Labels / badges: `0.6875rem` (11px), `font-weight: 500`, `uppercase`, `tracking-wide`.\n- Metadata: `0.75rem` (12px), `font-weight: 400`, `(--text-secondary)`.\n- No text gradients. No serif anywhere in UI.\n\n### Card Anatomy — Inspiration Card\nThe inspiration card is the core UI atom. It is portrait-oriented with these regions:\n1. **Image zone** (~68% of card height): The YouTube thumbnail fills the top with `object-cover`. Rounded top corners `(--radius-lg 0.5rem)`. Over the image: left/right chevron nav arrows (ghost circles, `opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100`, `150ms ease-out`). Bottom-left: category badge (small dark pill). Bottom-center: dot pagination. Top-right: `...` kebab button (always visible at low opacity, brightens on hover).\n2. **Content zone** (~32%): Dark `(--surface)` fill. `16px` horizontal padding, `12px` vertical. Video title in `(--text-primary)` at `font-weight: 600`, 2-line clamp. Channel name in `(--text-secondary)` at `0.75rem`.\n\n### Component Details\n\n**Badge/Tag pill**: `border-radius: 4px` (not full), `background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6)`, white text. For category: solid `(--primary)` background with white text. Padding `2px 8px`. Uppercase, tiny.\n\n**Kebab / context menu button**: `24px` circle, `border: 1px solid (--border)`, `background: (--surface)` at 80% opacity. On click, shows a floating dropdown panel `(--surface-raised)` with items: \"Copy link\", \"Add to collection\", \"Remove\", \"View channel\". Items are `32px` tall, `14px` text, icon+label rows. Destructive item (\"Remove\") in `(--primary)`.\n\n**Pagination dots**: 3 dots `4px` diameter. Active: `(--primary)`. Inactive: `oklch(0.95 0 0 / 0.3)`. Spacing `4px` apart.\n\n**Nav arrows**: `28px` circle, semi-transparent dark background, white chevron icon. Positioned absolutely at vertical center of image area, `8px` from edges.\n\n### Layout Signatures\n- Cards are `320px` wide with `aspect-ratio 16/9` thumbnail + `~100px` content zone.\n- In grid views: 3 columns on desktop, gap `16px`.\n- Hover raises border color from `(--border)` to `oklch(0.38 0 0)`. No scale or shadow change.\n- Dropdown opens below the kebab icon, aligned right, `4px` offset from button, `z-50`.\n\n### Spacing & Density\nTight. `16px` card padding, `8px` between image and title area, `4px` between title and meta. The card is intentionally compact — creators browse dozens of inspirations at once.\n\n### Motion & Interaction\nAll transitions `150ms ease-out`. Hover reveals are the primary interaction pattern: arrows and overlays fade in on card hover. Dropdown appears instantly (no animation needed). No zoom, no transform, no spring physics.\n\n### Overall Vibe\nProfessional creative tool. Every pixel earns its place. The darkness makes thumbnails pop. The red-orange primary makes actions feel urgent and branded. Grid lines and subtle borders provide structure without noise. Zero decorative elements — the art lives in the thumbnails.\n",
